INT. JURY ROOM - FLOODED COURTHOUSE - NIGHT

Two inches of black water on the floor. A long mahogany table above it. Five jurors sit with their feet on rungs, trousers rolled. A single lantern on the table.

HATTIE BOONE (60s, foreperson, cardigan, reading glasses) taps a verdict form. SUNIL RAO (30s, jacket on his head against the drip). BEVERLY OSEI (40s, nurse, arms crossed). ROMAN VOLKOV (50s, plumber, boots, a flask). ESTELLE FARRIER (70s, hat with a veil, hands folded).

HATTIE
We've been in here nine hours.

SUNIL
Ten.

BEVERLY
Eleven, if you count the lunch.

HATTIE
Nobody counts the lunch.

ROMAN
(raising the flask)
I count the lunch.

HATTIE
Roman.

ROMAN
It's water.

HATTIE
It isn't.

Hattie holds out her hand. Roman gives her the flask. She sniffs, wrinkles her nose, and sets it on the table.

HATTIE (CONT'D)
Show of hands. Guilty.

Sunil raises his. Roman raises his. Beverly does not. Estelle does not. Hattie does, slowly.

HATTIE (CONT'D)
Three to two.

BEVERLY
She did it.

ESTELLE
She did not.

SUNIL
Who? Who did it?

BEVERLY
The defendant, Sunil. The woman. She said it herself.

ESTELLE
She said she was sorry. That's not the same thing.

Water laps at the legs of the table. The lantern flickers. Hattie lifts her eyes, and stops.

HATTIE
Where is the foreman's chair?

They turn. At the head of the table, the chair is pulled out. Somebody has taken the sixth place. A wet gown lies folded on the seat. Nobody saw anyone enter.

ESTELLE
Oh, dear.

BEVERLY
Hattie. There's only five of us.

HATTIE
Count again.

SUNIL
One, two, three, four, five. Five.

ESTELLE
Six, dear. You forgot yourself.

Sunil looks down. His reflection in the black water, perfectly still, looks back up at him and does not blink.

SUNIL
Okay. I want to change my vote.
